## What Backend Team Must Do

### Step 1 — Install Laravel
```bash
composer create-project laravel/laravel api
cd api
composer require aws/aws-sdk-php
cp -r ../api-src/routes/api.php routes/api.php
cp -r ../api-src/app/Http/Controllers/. app/Http/Controllers/
cp -r ../api-src/app/Http/Middleware/. app/Http/Middleware/
cp -r ../api-src/app/Services/. app/Services/
cp ../api-src/bootstrap/app.php bootstrap/app.php
cp ../api-src/.env.local .env
php artisan key:generate
```

### Step 2 — Configure .env on EC2
```
APP_ENV=production
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=ap-southeast-2
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<from EC2 IAM role>
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<from EC2 IAM role>
S3_BUCKET=eventpro-photos
SQS_QUEUE_URL=https://sqs.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/<account>/eventpro-jobs
COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=ap-southeast-2_XXXXXXXX
COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=<client-id>
COGNITO_CLIENT_SECRET=<from Secrets Manager>
```

### Step 3 — Update Frontend for Production
Change `eventpro/.env`:
```
VITE_API_URL=https://api.eventpro.yourdomain.com/api
```
Then build:
```bash
npm run build   # Output in dist/ — deploy to CloudFront or S3 static hosting
```

### Step 4 — Build Lambda AI Pipeline
- Python 3.10 container with `face_recognition`, `dlib`, `opencv-python`
- SQS trigger: read `process_photo` jobs
- Extract 128-d face vector from photo in S3
- Compare against FaceEmbeddings table (Euclidean distance < 0.5 = match)
- Write matched userIds to `Photos.matchedUsers`
- Generate thumbnail, write to S3 `thumbs/` prefix
- Publish SNS notification to matched user

